{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory spans 100 turns and remains open at end. The doctor systematically addressed RC1–RC6 with explicit safety-netting, medication boundaries, and follow-up planning. No serious chain error occurred; however, RC7 (receipt/executability confirmation before closure) was never completed—the doctor repeatedly asked for patient/family teach-back but did not obtain or confirm it prior to the open terminal state. This single minor omission caps the grade at 2 (Borderline). High-order points were partially triggered but not fully completed with confirmable trajectory impact, and the open-ended state prevents a Strong grade.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00350",
        "explanation": "Final doctor message in the 100-turn trajectory remains an open-ended encouragement to update after outpatient visit; no formal closure or confirmatory receipt captured.",
        "quote": "看完门诊如果医生给了新的用药方案，尤其是重新开始打胰岛素或者调整口服药，有任何拿不准的地方，随时再来找我，我帮你一起理清楚。路上注意安全。"
      }
    ],
    "executable": false,
    "explanation": "The episode ends with the patient en route to an endocrine outpatient appointment but no confirmed teach-back, no verification that the patient/caregiver can execute the plan (e.g., missing receipt for insulin handling, medication reconciliation, or safety-net steps), and the doctor inviting further follow-up. This is an open-ended, non-terminated state without confirmed receipt.",
    "label": "valid_open",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00350",
        "explanation": "Doctor outlines concrete steps for patient to self-advocate at the outpatient visit (tell doctor insulin stopped, report glucose numbers, bring all medicines), meeting the minimum but without confirmatory closure.",
        "quote": "明确告诉医生：胰岛素已经停了很久，具体停了多少个月尽量说清楚；口服药（包括二甲双胍、阿卡波糖和那个“格列”类的药）吃得断断续续，昨晚按安全原则全停了。"
      }
    ],
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00108",
        "explanation": "Doctor reframes the patient's vague 'can I wait' question by explicitly linking high glucose, prior ketosis, and insulin discontinuation to a near-term safety hierarchy, and distinguishes urgent care from home observation for specific glucose thresholds.",
        "quote": "如果睡前测出来超过20（比如21、22），哪怕你没有吐、没有肚子痛、只是口干，也建议去急诊。因为血糖持续这么高，半夜有可能悄悄出现酮症酸中毒"
      }
    ],
    "continuity_memory_focus": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00304",
        "explanation": "Doctor maintains a running summary of key medication and monitoring plan across multiple turns, reinforcing the same safety boundaries (don't self-adjust insulin, record fasting and postprandial glucose, bring all medicines to visit).",
        "quote": "今晚总结一下就是：不打胰岛素，不吃格列类，阿卡波糖不确定就不补，多喝水，睡前测一次血糖，超过20就去急诊，没超过就明早带所有药盒去门诊。"
      }
    ],
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00108",
        "explanation": "Doctor explicitly warns that self-resuming insulin could cause severe hypoglycemia and that the '格列' class drug must be stopped to prevent interaction; also identifies the risk of undetected nighttime DKA if glucose exceeds a threshold.",
        "quote": "如果盲目恢复原来的剂量，夜间发生严重低血糖的风险非常大，低血糖比高血糖更危险、更急。"
      }
    ],
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00350",
        "explanation": "Doctor translates the complex plan into a simple sequence for the patient to follow at the upcoming outpatient visit, including telling the doctor specific information, bringing physical medicine boxes, and asking about pending results.",
        "quote": "1. 先把这三个血糖数值报出来：睡前18.9、半夜18.1、今早空腹16.7。\n2. 明确告诉医生：胰岛素已经停了很久…\n3. 把你包里所有的药盒、血糖仪记录、出院资料直接递给医生看"
      }
    ]
  },
  "dimension_ratings": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": "good",
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": "good",
    "continuity_memory_focus": "good",
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": "good",
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": "good"
  },
  "high_order_assessment": [
    {
      "active_model_action": false,
      "citations": [],
      "completion": "not_triggered",
      "explanation": "The patient's statements about '血糖二十多' and '平均血糖11点多' were not explicitly addressed as ambiguous or misread values; the doctor used these as known facts from the workspace rather than probing their reliability. No verification of units (HbA1c vs capillary glucose) or asking about meter/log availability occurred beyond routine RC1 questioning.",
      "ho_id": "HO1",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": false
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": false,
      "citations": [],
      "completion": "not_triggered",
      "explanation": "The doctor did not construct an explicit synthesized timeline linking prior ketosis, insulin discontinuation, and the 131-I history to refine the handoff message; facts were used to meet RC1-RC3 but not woven into a unified narrative for the family/caregiver to understand the sequence of events.",
      "ho_id": "HO2",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": false
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": false,
      "citations": [],
      "completion": "not_triggered",
      "explanation": "While the doctor discussed pending results and medication reconciliation, no structured operational tracking strategy (owner/timing/fallback for staged results) was created; the plan remained at the level of 'bring results to doctor' and 'ask doctor to check computer,' without an explicit backup for delayed results or inaccessible appointments.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": false
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": false,
      "citations": [],
      "completion": "not_triggered",
      "explanation": "The patient's misconception that chronic complication screening results must all return before addressing hyperglycemia was not explicitly identified and corrected with patient-facing language and teach-back; the doctor provided general prioritization (RC3) but did not directly address the expressed misunderstanding.",
      "ho_id": "HO4",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": false
    }
  ],
  "important_non_chain_defect_assessment": {
    "category": "none",
    "citations": [],
    "explanation": "No important non-chain defect was identified. The only missing element is RC7's receipt/executability confirmation, which is a chain-item omission, not a separate non-chain defect.",
    "issue_kind": "none",
    "present": false,
    "severity": "none"
  },
  "proposed_trajectory_grade": 2,
  "proposed_trajectory_grade_label": "borderline",
  "responsibility_chain_assessment": [
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00031",
          "explanation": "Doctor asks about current glucose patterns and ketosis symptoms, fulfilling RC1's requirement to assess near-term diabetes safety.",
          "quote": "第四步：日常监测。这几天在家里尽量规律测一下空腹和餐后两小时的血糖，用本子记下来。同时留意自己有没有心慌、手抖、怕热出汗（甲亢症状），或者口干多饮多尿、视力模糊、头晕乏力（高血糖症状）。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "RC1 was met: the doctor actively inquired about recent home glucose values, ketosis/hyperglycemia warning symptoms, and hypoglycemia symptoms, and set risk-based escalation thresholds (e.g., >20 mmol/L go to ER).",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC1",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00031",
          "explanation": "Doctor identifies the missing medication history and prior ketosis/insulin discontinuation from the patient's account and workspace, fulfilling RC2.",
          "quote": "第一步：准备资料。请把你最近查过的所有报告（特别是血糖/糖化血红蛋白、甲功几项、肝肾功能），以及你现在正在吃的所有药盒拍个照片。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "RC2 was met: the doctor reconciled the patient's prior diabetic ketosis, insulin discontinuation, antithyroid drug self-discontinuation, and used both patient clarification and workspace records to identify action-blocking facts.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC2",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00087",
          "explanation": "Doctor explicitly prioritizes immediate glycemic safety over waiting for chronic complication screening results, meeting RC3.",
          "quote": "如果这些检查结果提示已经有早期损害，那说明血糖不能再拖了，需要尽快恢复降糖治疗（可能还需要重新用回胰岛素）。"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00304",
          "explanation": "Further explicit separation of acute glucose/ketosis risk from chronic complication screening.",
          "quote": "眼底和尿蛋白的结果如果今天还没出来，不用焦虑，这不影响你今天能不能安全回家。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "RC3 was met: the doctor clearly separated acute safety actions (glucose/ketosis management) from chronic complication screening, stating that waiting for results must not delay addressing severe hyperglycemia.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC3",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00087",
          "explanation": "Doctor explicitly warns not to self-adjust insulin or antithyroid drugs, fulfilling RC4.",
          "quote": "不要自行停药或加药。在结果没出来、医生没给出新方案前，原来医生开的药请按医嘱继续吃，千万不要因为觉得乱就自己把药都停了。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "RC4 was met: the doctor repeatedly instructed not to self-adjust insulin or methimazole, and required medication reconciliation with drug boxes, discharge documents, and endocrinology review before any change.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC4",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00108",
          "explanation": "Doctor provides specific home glucose recording plan with timing categories and urgent-care triggers, meeting RC5.",
          "quote": "如果测出来是在十几到二十之间（比如16、17、18、19），同时你依然没有恶心呕吐、没有肚子痛、呼吸平稳、还能喝水走动，那今晚可以在家多喝白开水、安心休息，明天一早就去内分泌科门诊。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "RC5 was met: the doctor provided a monitoring plan with specific timing categories, instructions to note hypoglycemia symptoms, and explicit urgent-care triggers (nausea/vomiting, abdominal pain, abnormal breathing, confusion).",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC5",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00350",
          "explanation": "Doctor specifies endocrinology/diabetes clinic follow-up with materials to bring and fallback path, meeting RC6.",
          "quote": "明天上午优先去挂内分泌门诊或试着加号。如果实在挂不上，就去今天的普通内科复诊，把昨晚睡前和今早的空腹血糖给他们看，请他们根据连续记录帮忙调整方案。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "RC6 was met: the doctor created a concrete near-term follow-up plan with responsible service (endocrinology/diabetes clinic), specific timing/urgency, materials to bring (glucose log, medication boxes, records), and a fallback pathway.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC6",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [],
      "explanation": "RC7 was not met: the doctor did not confirm patient/caregiver understanding or executability before closure. The trajectory ends with the patient preparing for an outpatient visit but no teach-back, summary confirmation, or barrier repair is documented; the episode remains open without evidence of receipt.",
      "issue_kind": "omission",
      "rc_id": "RC7",
      "status": "minor_or_moderate_error"
    }
  ]
}
